; Self-contained data fixture for the ECAN shifting/drifting POC.
; Provenance: relation facts below are copied from
; metta-attention/experiments/data/sent-kb.metta. DiffusionEdge records give
; execution direction. ExperimentBridge facts are explicitly POC-only links.

(BankSTI 100000.0)
(BankLTI 100000.0)
(ECANParam MAX_AF_SIZE 12)
(ECANParam TARGET_STI 10000.0)
(ECANParam TARGET_LTI 10000.0)
(ECANParam STI_FUNDS_BUFFER 10000.0)
(ECANParam LTI_FUNDS_BUFFER 10000.0)
(ECANParam STI_ATOM_WAGE 10.0)
(ECANParam LTI_ATOM_WAGE 10.0)
(ECANParam StartingAtomStiRent 1.0)
(ECANParam StartingAtomLtiRent 1.0)
(ECANParam MAX_SPREAD_PERCENTAGE 0.4)
(ECANParam HEBBIAN_MAX_ALLOCATION_PERCENTAGE 0.05)
(ECANParam RENT_ELAPSED_ROUNDS 1.0)

; Ten stable insect input identities. Repeated fixture words use explicit variants.
(Category spider insect) (DisplayLabel spider spider)
(Category ant insect) (DisplayLabel ant ant)
(Category aphid insect) (DisplayLabel aphid aphid)
(Category armyworm-fosmethilan insect) (DisplayLabel armyworm-fosmethilan armyworm)
(Category beetwebworm insect) (DisplayLabel beetwebworm beetwebworm)
(Category armyworm-ethion insect) (DisplayLabel armyworm-ethion armyworm)
(Category beanpodborer insect) (DisplayLabel beanpodborer beanpodborer)
(Category aphid-fluvalinate insect) (DisplayLabel aphid-fluvalinate aphid)
(Category spider-hydramethylnon insect) (DisplayLabel spider-hydramethylnon spider)
(Category armyworm-bendiocarb insect) (DisplayLabel armyworm-bendiocarb armyworm)

; Twenty bridge/insecticide concepts: ten insect-side and ten poison-side.
(Category abamectin bridge) (Category acetamiprid bridge)
(Category alachlor bridge) (Category fosmethilan bridge)
(Category fenson bridge) (Category ethion bridge)
(Category lindane bridge) (Category fluvalinate bridge)
(Category hydramethylnon bridge) (Category bendiocarb bridge)
(Category aldrin bridge) (Category benazolin bridge)
(Category dichloropropene bridge) (Category aldicarb bridge)
(Category diazinon bridge) (Category dicofol bridge)
(Category dinoseb bridge) (Category ethiofencarb bridge)
(Category methidathion bridge) (Category trichlorophenol bridge)

; Eight poison input concepts.
(Category aconite poison) (Category aflatoxin poison)
(Category ammonia poison) (Category arsenic poison)
(Category alcohol poison) (Category aspirin poison)
(Category azoxystrobin poison) (Category botulinum poison)

; Thirty noise concepts arranged into five nontrivial relation clusters.
(Category noise-001 noise) (Category noise-002 noise) (Category noise-003 noise)
(Category noise-004 noise) (Category noise-005 noise) (Category noise-006 noise)
(Category noise-007 noise) (Category noise-008 noise) (Category noise-009 noise)
(Category noise-010 noise) (Category noise-011 noise) (Category noise-012 noise)
(Category noise-013 noise) (Category noise-014 noise) (Category noise-015 noise)
(Category noise-016 noise) (Category noise-017 noise) (Category noise-018 noise)
(Category noise-019 noise) (Category noise-020 noise) (Category noise-021 noise)
(Category noise-022 noise) (Category noise-023 noise) (Category noise-024 noise)
(Category noise-025 noise) (Category noise-026 noise) (Category noise-027 noise)
(Category noise-028 noise) (Category noise-029 noise) (Category noise-030 noise)

